# The entire footprint Unihelm has on Apache's own configuration: one include.
#
# Everything the panel writes lives under {{ apache_dir }}/ and is generated.
# This file exists so the panel never has to edit apache2.conf, sites-available,
# sites-enabled or any file the distribution owns — which is what makes
# `apt upgrade apache2` and a panel upgrade independent of each other. `a2ensite`
# is never run for the same reason: a symlink farm is a second place for a vhost
# to be half removed from.
#
# `IncludeOptional`, not `Include`: an empty or missing directory is a fatal
# error for the latter, and this file is written before the first vhost is.
IncludeOptional {{ apache_dir }}/*.conf

# OCSP stapling needs a cache, and the cache is server-scope.
#
# `SSLUseStapling on` inside a vhost — which every TLS site this panel writes
# carries — is not enough on its own: without a cache Apache refuses the
# configuration outright (AH02172). Every machine with a TLS site would have
# failed its own configtest at the last step of a switch, which is safe and
# also means the switch could never have completed on a real server.
#
# Server scope is why it lives in this file rather than in the site template:
# the directive is not allowed inside `<VirtualHost>`, and one cache is shared
# by every site anyway.
#
# `<IfModule>` because this file is included whether or not mod_ssl is loaded,
# and an unknown directive is a fatal error rather than a warning.
<IfModule ssl_module>
    SSLStaplingCache shmcb:${APACHE_RUN_DIR}/unihelm_ssl_stapling(65536)
</IfModule>
